<?phem

namespace App\Ui\Demos;

use Phem\Attribute\Page;
use Phem\Node;
use Phem\Ui\Base\Examples\{AutocompleteAsyncDemo, AutocompleteGridDemo, AutocompleteVirtualizedDemo};

use function App\Ui\{DemoPage, Example, Examples, Hero};
use function Phem\Ui\Base\Examples\{AutocompleteAutoHighlightDemo, AutocompleteCommandPaletteDemo, AutocompleteFuzzyDemo, AutocompleteGroupedDemo, AutocompleteHeroDemo, AutocompleteInlineDemo, AutocompleteLimitDemo};

#[Page('/components/autocomplete')]
function AutocompletePage(): Node
{
    return (
        <DemoPage slug="autocomplete">
            <Hero source="AutocompleteHeroDemo">
                <AutocompleteHeroDemo />
            </Hero>
            <Examples>
                <Example title="Async search" source="AutocompleteAsyncDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Load items asynchronously while typing and render custom status content. The <code>onChange</code> handler of <code>ComboboxInput</code> calls a repository service, and <code>ComboboxStatus</code> shows the state of the search: a spinner while it runs, the number of results, no match, or an error. Type "will_error" to see a failure.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteAsyncDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Inline autocomplete" source="AutocompleteInlineDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Autofill the input with the highlighted item while navigating with arrow keys using the <code>mode</code> prop. Accepts <code>aria-autocomplete</code> values <code>list</code>, <code>both</code>, <code>inline</code>, or <code>none</code>.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteInlineDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Grouped" source="AutocompleteGroupedDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Organize related options with <code>ComboboxGroup</code> and <code>ComboboxGroupLabel</code> to add section headings inside the popup.</p>
                        <p>Render one group for each section of your data, with the heading text in its label and its items in it. A group with no matching item is hidden.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteGroupedDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Fuzzy matching" source="AutocompleteFuzzyDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Use fuzzy matching to find relevant results even when the query doesn’t exactly match the item text. Here <code>filter="fuzzy"</code> matches the characters of the query in order, in the label and in each of the <code>keywords</code> of an item, and <code>ComboboxHighlight</code> marks the text that has the query.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteFuzzyDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Limit results" source="AutocompleteLimitDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Limit the number of visible items using the <code>limit</code> prop and guide users to refine their query using <code>ComboboxStatus</code>.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteLimitDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Auto highlight" source="AutocompleteAutoHighlightDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>The first matching item can be automatically highlighted as the user types by specifying the <code>autoHighlight</code> prop on <code>Autocomplete</code>. Set the prop’s value to <code>"always"</code> if the highlight should always be present, such as when the list is rendered inline within a dialog.</p>
                        <p>The prop can be combined with the <code>keepHighlight</code> and <code>highlightItemOnHover</code> props to configure how the highlight behaves during mouse interactions.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteAutoHighlightDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Command palette" source="AutocompleteCommandPaletteDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Use the autocomplete input to filter a list of command items that perform an action when clicked. With no <code>ComboboxPopup</code>, the list is inline and always open. Give the items <code>data-phem-dialog-target="close"</code> to close the dialog on a choice. Each open starts with an empty search.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteCommandPaletteDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Grid layout" source="AutocompleteGridDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Display items in a grid layout, wrapping each row in <code>ComboboxRow</code> components, and add the <code>grid</code> prop to <code>Autocomplete</code>. The arrow keys move in the rows and in the columns.</p>
                        <p>The browser filters the emojis, and the matches of each category fill its rows again. Give the root <code>insertInto</code> with the id of a text field: a choice inserts the <code>value</code> of the item at the caret of the field, and the focus goes back to the field.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteGridDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Virtualized" source="AutocompleteVirtualizedDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Efficiently handle large datasets by rendering only the first matches. The <code>onChange</code> handler of <code>ComboboxInput</code> searches the dataset on the server, and the state keeps the first 50 matches. <code>ComboboxStatus</code> shows the number of matches, and a choice writes the <code>label</code> of the item in the input.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AutocompleteVirtualizedDemo />
                </Example>
            </Examples>
        </DemoPage>
    );
}
